course: dictionary
lesson: 11703
title: Giving credit with attribution
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Attribution means saying who wrote, made, said or did something. It is the credit you give to the person who made it. When you use a picture, a quote or a fact from someone else, you give attribution by saying where it came from.
explain: «Mrs Patel showed us a photo of a snow leopard and said, "Photo by Amir Khan."» The name Amir Khan is the attribution: it tells us who took the photo. Leaving the name out, as if the photo were yours, is not fair.
explain: Attribution can also mean saying what caused something. «The attribution of the flood to heavy rain» means the flood was blamed on heavy rain. Art experts argue about the attribution of a painting to a painter, because they want to know who really painted it.
fact: Attribution means giving credit: saying who wrote, made, said or did something.
fact: «With attribution» means you say where something came from. «Without attribution» means you do not say.
fact: «Give attribution» means name the source, and «correct attribution» means naming the right person or place.
fact: Attribution can also mean saying what caused something, as in «the attribution of the flood to heavy rain».
fact: In a formal sense, attribution means a quality that someone is thought to have.
exercise: «The photo was taken by Ellie Brown, so the caption gives her attribution.» What does attribution mean here? | Making the photo much brighter | *Saying who took the photo | Printing the photo in colour | Hiding the photo in a drawer
exercise: Sam copied a poem from a book and said it was his own. What should he have given? | A new picture | A bigger font | *Attribution, by naming the poet | A longer title
exercise: Which phrase means you did name where a quote came from? | No credit at all | *With attribution | Attribution removed | Without attribution
test: «The attribution of the flood to heavy rain» means: | Drawing rain on paper | Stopping the rain | Making a map of the flood | *Saying that heavy rain caused the flood
test: The school play used a song, but the programme had no attribution. What was missing? | The date of the play | *The name of who wrote the song | The colour of the lights | The price of the tickets
exam: "Correct attribution" means: | Being very quick to finish | Copying something exactly with no name | Choosing the best colour for a picture | *Naming the right person or place a thing came from
